  description="Terms of use for isithot.today. Forecasts are estimates and not for safety-critical decisions."
>
  <h1>Terms</h1>
  <p>
    <em>Draft for review. Last updated 6 October 2026.</em>
  </p>

  <h2>Forecasts are estimates</h2>
  <p>
    isithot.today summarises computer forecasts from several weather models. Forecasts can be wrong,
    and "hot" is a judgement, not a measurement. Do not rely on this site for safety-critical
    decisions, including heat health, outdoor work, travel or events. Follow advice from your
    national weather service and health authorities.
  </p>

  <h2>Use of the site</h2>
  <p>
    You may use the site for personal, non-commercial purposes. Please do not scrape it or call its
    API at volume; requests are rate-limited.
  </p>

  <h2>Data and credits</h2>
  <p>
    Forecast data from Open-Meteo.com (CC BY 4.0). Climate data from NASA POWER. Place names from
    GeoNames (CC BY 4.0). Links to BBC Weather, the Met Office and AccuWeather are provided for
    convenience; we are not affiliated with them.
  </p>

  <h2>Liability</h2>
  <p>
    The site is provided as is, without warranties. To the extent the law allows, we are not liable
    for losses arising from its use.
  </p>
</Content>
